      "message": "Hi Andrew, \n\nBefore I go further, it would be great if you can tell me if this is a sound approach or not.\n\nI actually don\u0027t like the dup_from_raw approach. When I followed that approach, I see that I am creating many fds unnecessarily. In addition, it breaks some places like authfs where rawfd \u003d\u003d ownedfd.as_raw_fd() is assumed (which IMO is a valid assumption).\n\nSo, I came up with this idea that we pre-create OwnedFds for inherited FDs by reading /proc/self/fd/* (of course that part has to be unsafe). Then conversion from RawFd to OwnedFd would be just giving the ownership of one of the pre-created OwnedFds.\n\nWDYT?",
